<%# Back control for a submission's detail page. Belongs inside the page's
    .form-header, where it pins to the top left and mirrors .form-header__action
    on the right — see components/_forms.scss.

    It steps back through browser history, so it returns the viewer to whichever
    list they arrived from (the inbox, Submissions, a search result) rather than
    guessing. With no history to step back to — a link opened in a fresh tab or
    pasted in — the href carries them to Submissions, where every submission
    lives regardless of its status.

    Render it with: render "shared/back_button"
-%>
<%= link_to "← Back", submissions_path,
      class: "btn ghost compact form-header__back",
      data: { controller: "back-link", action: "back-link#navigate" } %>
